  "answer": "The official pricing policy is the 2026 schedule, effective June 1, 2026, and it fully supersedes and replaces the deprecated 2025 pricing proposal [NL-003#NL-003-S08]. The 2025 proposal is obsolete, was never adopted as the long-term model, and must not be used in active agreements [NL-004#NL-004-S02] [NL-004#NL-004-S01].\n\nComparison of official 2026 pricing vs. deprecated 2025 proposal [NL-004#NL-004-S05]:\n- **Starter Plan**: $1,200/month (2026) vs. $900/month (2025); onboarding fee $2,500 vs. $1,500.\n- **Growth Plan**: $3,600/month (2026) vs. $2,800/month (2025); onboarding fee $7,500 vs. $4,500.\n- **Enterprise Plan**: From $8,500/month (2026) vs. From $6,000/month (2025); onboarding fee minimum $15,000 vs. From $10,000.\n\nThe 2025 proposal also specified included learners/admin seats: Starter 500 learners/3 admin seats; Growth 2,000 learners/10 admin seats; Enterprise custom/custom [NL-004#NL-004-S02]. The 2026 policy is the sole source of truth for sales, renewals, and audits [NL-003#NL-003-S01], and legacy 2025 contracts must migrate to 2026 rates at renewal, with a possible one-time 90-day grace period at a mid-tier rate for qualifying accounts, subject to CSM request and VP approval [NL-003#NL-003-S08].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
